<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened runtime entitlements for the distributable macOS app.

  Notarization requires the hardened runtime, and the hardened runtime turns
  off several things a PyInstaller-packaged Python app relies on. Each key
  here is present because leaving it out breaks a specific thing, not as a
  precaution.

  device.bluetooth: the strap. NSBluetoothAlwaysUsageDescription in the
  Info.plist is necessary but not sufficient under the hardened runtime.
  Without this entitlement CoreBluetooth is refused and the app finds no
  devices at all, with no error that says why.

  disable-library-validation: a onedir bundle loads dozens of .so and .dylib
  files at runtime. Library validation requires every one of them to be
  signed by the same team ID, and the wheels they came from are not. Without
  this the app dies on its first extension-module import.

  allow-jit and allow-unsigned-executable-memory: ctypes and libffi build
  call thunks in memory and execute them, which the hardened runtime blocks
  by default. bleak reaches CoreBluetooth through pyobjc, which is ctypes
  all the way down.

  What is deliberately absent is get-task-allow, which lets a debugger
  attach and which the notary service rejects outright.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.bluetooth</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>

    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
